Let $a$ and $b$ be two integers, at least one of which is non-zero. The \textbf{greatest common divisor} (GCD) of $a$ and $b$, denoted by $\gcd(a,b)$ or $(a,b)$, is the largest positive integer $d$ that satisfies:

\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*), leftmargin=*]
    \item $d > 0$
    \item $d | a$ and $d | b$
    \item If $c | a$ and $c | b$, then $c | d$
\end{enumerate}

